204:### 2.8 Prompt-stack guide reflection / benchmark maintenance
205-
206-Use when:
207-- an attached guide, canon, or pattern document is the comparison target
208-- the task is to check whether actual prompt docs still reflect that governing source
--
222-- `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay` when disclosure, mutation, or approval risk changes the benchmark path
223-
224-Typical packets:
225-- `Benchmark registry memo` for chapter-family inventory, cohort scope, or expected packet floor
226:- `Guide reflection benchmark memo` for question -> answer -> verification -> patch-target loops
227-- `Prompt-stack release review` when the benchmark is deciding release, rewrite acceptance, or parity preservation
228-- `Packet compliance report` when packet-floor doctrine or omission findings are the live surface
229-- `Context sufficiency review memo` or `Critique quality review memo` when weak context or no-gain iteration may explain benchmark instability
230-
231-Escalate to stronger operational artifacts when:
232:- document parity is no longer the live question and assembled prompt behavior must be replayed
233-- scenario lineage, run linkage, or replay execution state must stay inspectable across reruns
234-- the verdict depends on whether a replay actually executed rather than whether a benchmark question set exists
235-
236-Preferred operational artifacts:
237:- `Benchmark cohort manifest` when scenario identity and expected replay contract must be fixed before execution
238:- `Replay runner verdict sheet` when runner state, partial completion, or replay-attempted vs replay-complete distinction is the live issue
239:- `Replay suite verdict memo` when a higher-level suite verdict must summarize multiple runner-linked replay outcomes without hiding partial coverage
