243-## 3. Control-Packet Mapping
--
270-- process-quality or replay-safe inspection -> `Safe trajectory artifact report`
271-- tool regression or deterministic harness evaluation -> `Mock-tool evaluation report`
272-- bounded multi-view challenge -> `Debate / consensus comparison memo`
273-- prompt-stack rewrite or release audit -> `Prompt-stack release review`
274:- guide-chapter reflection or doc-to-runtime parity benchmark -> `Guide reflection benchmark memo`
275:- assembled prompt replay setup -> `Benchmark cohort manifest`
276:- assembled prompt replay runner-state verdict -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`
277:- assembled prompt replay suite summary -> `Replay suite verdict memo`
278-- governance-owned packet-floor audit or omission-sensitive review -> `Packet compliance report`
279-- versioned replay suite or benchmark cohort definition -> `Benchmark registry memo`
280-- context-pack sufficiency or stale-context review -> `Context sufficiency review memo`
281-- critique-loop quality or no-gain-loop review -> `Critique quality review memo`
282-- adaptation promotion or rollback gate -> `Adaptation promotion review memo`
283-- route, prioritization, or exploration scoring -> `Route-quality scorecard`
284-- repo-scale coding scenario and verification-running contract -> `Coding benchmark scenario memo`
285-- executed benchmark result or cohort verdict -> `Benchmark execution report`
286:- replay execution verdict -> `Replay suite verdict memo`
287-- context failure and substrate diagnosis -> `Context failure taxonomy memo`
288-- critique utility and refinement delta review -> `Critique utility scorecard`
289-- adaptation lifecycle and rollback state -> `Adaptation lifecycle state memo`
290-- route-switch and re-prioritization audit -> `Route re-prioritization audit memo`
291-- engineering proof packet with executed-vs-unexecuted state -> `Coding proof bundle memo`
292-- integrated promotion packet with confidence class -> `Release evidence bundle v2`
293-- telemetry trend and cohort-aware drift review -> `Telemetry trend memo`
294:- benchmark cohort identity and run-linkage packet -> `Benchmark cohort manifest`
295:- replay execution-sheet and runner linkage packet -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`
296-- context substrate scoring packet -> `Context substrate scorecard`
297-- critique delta and no-gain logging packet -> `Critique delta ledger`
298-- adaptation controller audit packet -> `Adaptation controller audit packet`
299-- route-switch benchmark packet -> `Route-switch benchmark verdict`
--
317-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
318-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
319-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
320-- Guardrails / Safety -> `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay`
321:- Evaluation / Monitoring -> `PROMPT_evaluation_monitoring_overlay` + `eval-ops`; prefer `Benchmark registry memo`, `Guide reflection benchmark memo`, or `Prompt-stack release review`
322-
323-Lookup rule:
324-- if a chapter family can only be answered by operator-facing prose and not by the active runtime / skill surface, treat that as a reflection gap and patch the actual prompt docs before claiming parity
325-
--
339-- distinguish `light review memo`, `stronger packet`, and `operational artifact` rather than treating every packet as equal-strength evidence
340-- if a lighter memo and a stronger artifact address the same control problem, keep the stronger artifact active and background or supersede the lighter memo
341-- if the task has crossed from packet presence review into operational proof review, prefer the stronger operational artifact and mark weaker packets as superseded rather than silently doubling them
342-- if two compatible artifacts share one lineage, let the newer artifact supersede the stale predecessor explicitly
343:- treat `Benchmark cohort manifest`, `Replay runner verdict sheet`, `Adaptation controller audit packet`, `Coding benchmark execution ledger`, `Release promotion decision record`, `Telemetry drift investigation memo`, `Route-switch benchmark verdict`, and `Context substrate scorecard` as the direct packet floor before benchmark-grade, replay-grade, controller-grade, coding-proof-grade, release-grade, drift-grade, route-quality-grade, or retrieval-substrate-grade language
344-- keep shared identifiers such as `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable whenever benchmark, replay, adaptation, release, or telemetry packets must be linked across rounds
345-- when artifacts are joined, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness first; reject incompatible merges and preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in the surviving artifact
346-- keep failure classes such as `false-promotion`, `false-hold`, `drift-triggered review`, `rollback aftermath`, `route-switch failure`, `late clarification`, and `failed fallback timing` independently diagnosable when those control surfaces are active
347-- keep `runner readiness failure`, `partial completion`, `quarantine entry`, `freshness defect`, and `unresolved join failure` independently visible when they drive escalation, downgrade, split verdict retention, or join rejection
