432-Mock-tool discipline:
433-- when validating agentic tool behavior, prefer mock tools or a dedicated safe test environment over live irreversible systems
434-- check parameter construction, partial-state handling, and result-interpretation separately when the workflow is non-deterministic
435-- if a coding or workflow benchmark depends on command execution, keep the verification-running policy explicit and separate from tool availability
436:- benchmark pressure does not convert missing substrate, blocked commands, or unavailable harnesses into silent success
437-- if benchmark or replay execution depends on a harness, keep harness readiness and harness absence separate from tool correctness itself
438-- when tool-mediated benchmark execution is the real evidence surface, prefer a compact `Benchmark execution report` over generic success narration
439-- when replayability across tool runs is the active decision boundary, prefer a `Replay suite verdict memo` that keeps replay execution state explicit
440-- if tool-assisted coding proof is claimed, keep the executed-vs-unexecuted boundary visible and prefer a `Coding proof bundle memo` instead of collapsing tool-call success into code correctness
