880:- if runner or harness evidence is absent, do not let a benchmark, replay, or coding-proof packet overclaim actual execution strength
881-- keep `runner readiness failure`, `partial completion`, and `failed fallback timing` independently visible when tool-mediated failure diagnosis is the real issue
882-- before joining runner artifacts with broader proof packets, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness; reject incompatible merges that would overstate actual execution
883-- preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in any joined tool-execution artifact that survives reconciliation
