308-
309-When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
310-
311-- Prompt Chaining / Planning -> base prompts; keep staged dependency, checkpoint, and fallback visibility explicit instead of collapsing into one-shot execution language
312-- Routing / Prioritization / Exploration -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo` or `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`
313:- Parallelization / Multi-Agent / A2A -> `PROMPT_multi_agent_overlay` + `orchestration-control`; prefer `Delegation admission memo`, `A2A task-handoff memo`, and `Join-quality review memo`
314-- Tool Use / MCP -> `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay`; prefer `Tool capability contract / precondition memo` or `MCP capability handoff memo`
315-- Memory / Learning / Adaptation -> `PROMPT_memory_adaptation_overlay`; prefer `Memory scope / checkpoint profile memo`, `Learning-signal review memo`, and `Adaptation decision memo`
316-- Goal / Monitoring / Recovery / HITL -> base prompts; prefer `Goal-monitoring status memo`, `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`, and `HITL approval packet`
317-- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
318-- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
319-- Reasoning Techniques / Reflection -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Critique quality review memo` when critique utility or no-gain loops are under review
